  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does National Aeronautics and Space Administration spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $15.4B in FY2026 to date. The agency placed 8,076 awards with an average award size of $1.9M, and obligations were down 2.5% year over year. Fiscal year obligations were $15B in FY21, $15.2B in FY22, $16.1B in FY23, $15B in FY24, and $15.8B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does National Aeronautics and Space Administration buy?",
      "a": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration buys research and development, space vehicle manufacturing, engineering services, facilities support, and construction. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) totaled $5.6B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing totaled $3.2B, Engineering Services totaled $796M, Facilities Support Services totaled $640M, and Industrial Building Construction totaled $596M in FY2026 to date."
